-- vmu-nouns: the nouns of sections 1 to 12 of the Monetary Units Act 2004 (Victoria), and nothing else.
-- Types only: no rule and no directive.
-- Each type is a fact that a witness of ordinary competence could state about an instrument or a regulation.
-- Whether the thing falls under a rule of the Act is a rule, and is in the module of the section that says so.

-- The kinds of instrument that sections 4, 7, 8 and 10 name: "an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument".
-- `an instrument of another kind` stands for any instrument that is none of the three; the text gives no rule for it.
-- src:53 | If in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument there is a statement of a number (whether whole, fractional or decimal) of what are called fee units, that statement must, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as stating a number of dollars equal to the product obtained by multiplying the number of fee units by the amount fixed from time to time by the Treasurer under section 5(3).
@ref s 4 (src:53)
DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `an Act`
    `a statutory rule`
    `a legislative instrument`
    `an instrument of another kind`

-- What the Treasurer fixes: "a fee or penalty unit" and "an annual rate" (section 12).
-- "something else" stands for any other fixing; the text gives no rule for it.
-- src:128 | (a) a fee or penalty unit in accordance with section 5 or 11; or
-- src:129 | (b) an annual rate in accordance with section 5 or 11.
@ref s 12(a), s 12(b) (src:128-129)
DECLARE `Thing fixed` IS ONE OF
    `a fee unit`
    `a penalty unit`
    `an annual rate`
    `something else`

-- The purposes for which regulations may be made, as paragraphs (a) to (g) of section 9(1) list them.
-- `a purpose not listed in section 9(1)` stands for any other purpose.
-- src:86 | (1) The Governor in Council, on the certificate and recommendation of the Treasurer, may make regulations amending any statutory rule made under any Act to—
-- src:87 | (a) convert any fees specified in monetary amounts in the statutory rule to fee units;
-- src:88 | (b) convert any penalties specified in monetary amounts in the statutory rule to penalty units;
-- src:89 | (c) convert any fee units or penalty units specified or referred to in the statutory rule to fee units or penalty units calculated in accordance with this Act;
-- src:90 | (d) convert the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit specified or referred to in the statutory rule to the equivalent monetary amount of that fee unit or penalty unit calculated in accordance with this Act;
-- src:91 | (e) convert any fee units specified in the statutory rule to fees specified in monetary amounts;
-- src:92 | (f) convert any penalty units specified in the statutory rule to penalties in monetary amounts;
-- src:93 | (g) increase any fees specified in monetary amounts in the statutory rule by the amount of the cumulative annual rates fixed by the Treasurer under this Act for the period that the fee has had effect without any increase.
@ref s 9(1), s 9(1)(a), s 9(1)(b), s 9(1)(c), s 9(1)(d), s 9(1)(e), s 9(1)(f), s 9(1)(g) (src:86-93)
DECLARE `Head of section 9(1)` IS ONE OF
    `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units`
    `converting penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units`
    `converting fee units or penalty units to fee units or penalty units calculated in accordance with the Act`
    `converting the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit to the equivalent monetary amount calculated in accordance with the Act`
    `converting fee units to fees in monetary amounts`
    `converting penalty units to penalties in monetary amounts`
    `increasing fees in monetary amounts by the cumulative annual rates`
    `a purpose not listed in section 9(1)`

-- What the Treasurer may certify under section 9(2): the conversion that the regulation makes,
-- one constructor for each of the cases of paragraphs (a)(i) to (h).
-- src:94 | (2) Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 does not apply to a regulation made under this section if the Treasurer certifies in writing that—
-- src:95 | (a) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(a)—
-- src:96 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by $10; or
-- src:97 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- src:98 | (b) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(b)—
-- src:99 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by $100; or
-- src:100 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by the value of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- src:101 | (c) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(c), the regulation converts fee units to the equivalent number of fee units having regard to the current value of a fee unit under this Act;
-- src:102 | (d) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(c), the regulation converts penalty units to the equivalent number of penalty units having regard to the current value of a penalty unit under this Act;
-- src:103 | (e) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(d), the regulation converts the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit specified or referred to in the statutory rule to the equivalent monetary amount of that fee unit or penalty unit under this Act;
-- src:104 | (f) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(e), the regulation converts fee units to fees in monetary amounts by multiplying the amount of the fee unit by the value of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- src:105 | (g) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(f), the regulation converts penalty units to penalties in monetary amounts by multiplying the amount of the penalty unit by the value of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- src:106 | (h) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(g), the regulation increases any fees that are less than the value of one fee unit by an amount not exceeding the cumulative annual rates fixed by the Treasurer under this Act for the period that the fee has had effect without any increase.
@ref s 9(2) (src:94-106)
DECLARE `Conversion certified` IS ONE OF
    `dividing the fee by 10 dollars`
    `dividing the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)`
    `dividing the penalty by 100 dollars`
    `dividing the penalty by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)`
    `converting fee units to the equivalent number of fee units having regard to the current value of a fee unit`
    `converting penalty units to the equivalent number of penalty units having regard to the current value of a penalty unit`
    `converting the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit to the equivalent monetary amount under the Act`
    `multiplying the amount of the fee unit by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)`
    `multiplying the amount of the penalty unit by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)`
    `increasing fees less than the value of one fee unit by an amount not exceeding the cumulative annual rates`
    `some other conversion`
